Suppose that a molecule has several probable structures each of which belongs to a different point group. Then the number of infrared and Raman-active fundamentals should be different for each structure. Therefore the most probable model can be selected by comparing the observed number of infrared-and Raman-active fundamentals with that predicted theoretically for each model. text
Consider the
equation_inline
