text
molecule as an example. It may be tetrahedral or square-planar. By use of the methods described in the preceding sections, the number of infrared or Raman-active fundamentals can be found easily for each structure. Tables I-9a and I-9b summarize the results. It is seen that the tetrahedral structure predicts two infrared-active fundamentals (one stretching and one bending), whereas the square-planar structure predicts three infrared-active fundamentals (one stretching and two bendings). The infrared spectrum of
equation_inline
XeF_{4}
text
in the vapor phase exhibits one XeF stretching at
equation_inline
586\ cm^{-1}
text
