equation_inline
3750 \, cm^{-1}
text
, while a water molecule with two nearest neighbors may absorb light at
equation_inline
3751 \, cm^{-1}
text
. Samples with strong intermolecular interactions have more chemical environments than samples with weak intermolecular interactions because electronic effects are greater for strong interactions. Thus, a non-polar molecule like hexane has fewer chemical environments than a polar molecule like water. The more chemical environments a sample has, the more

